{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788087222510593001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"floating-chromium-leafwing","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"541e0e81247a124211ec46f94e684376ebe9e40af25bbd2c8fc1b2a489da9353","event_uuid":"04953580-58b8-4205-9b6c-5c7b9a350074","position":{"commit_sha":"47f628bacafb665a0fdbc6d5ddbb0eca231941a9","position":"1788078144998216587-04953580-58b8-4205-9b6c-5c7b9a350074"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"959bfb73d2749222b65a322f306b6343ec7d94ff568613cfb35babc63ded9954","event_uuid":"a815aebe-b319-4319-a886-291b6317e153","position":{"commit_sha":"80226dce055b4fd106692b99f7aebd40cda79d40","position":"1788078165355608625-a815aebe-b319-4319-a886-291b6317e153"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788078144998216587,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"a815aebe-b319-4319-a886-291b6317e153","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"e3e0-2e7c-b280-4b4a"}],"description":"## Problem\n\nSurfaced while fixing `anatomical-arbored-oyster` (e3e0-2e7c-b280-4b4a). Once that fix removed the `FileNotFoundError` collection error (macOS leg) and the `license-files` build `TypeError` (floor leg), the `Test Suite (mirror)` legs run to completion and reveal a large, **pre-existing** failure class that was previously masked.\n\nDominant macOS-leg error (~90 failures across `test_provider_parity`, `test_transport_retry`, `test_llm_fallback_chain`, `test_llm_provider_factory`, `test_llm_timeouts`, `test_web_tool_gating`, `test_llm_config_gate_root`, ...):\n\n```\nError: Invalid `http_client` argument; Expected an instance of `httpx2.AsyncClient` but got <class 'httpx.AsyncClient'>\n```\n\n## Root cause\n\n`pyproject.toml` declares `pydantic-ai-slim[anthropic,retries,duckduckgo]>=1.107,<2` but places **no upper bound on the `anthropic` SDK itself**. The mirror sweep installs UNLOCKED:\n- `sweep (macos, full suite)`: `uv pip install '.[dev,reviewbot,ui]'` (non-editable)\n- `sweep (declared lower-bound resolution)`: `uv pip install --resolution lowest-direct '.[dev,agents]'`\n\nBoth resolve `anthropic==1.2.0`, whose client vendors `httpx2` and **rejects** a stdlib `httpx.AsyncClient`. rebar's provider seam (`src/rebar/llm/anthropic_model.py:_build_retrying_anthropic_provider` -> `anthropic/_client.py:__init__`) passes an `httpx.AsyncClient`, so construction raises `TypeError` and cascades into every Anthropic-touching test. The Verified merge gate is green because `uv.lock` pins an older, compatible anthropic; only the unlocked sweep legs float to 1.2.0.\n\n## Fix direction (DESIGN — needs decision)\n\nEither (a) add an `anthropic` upper-bound/pin compatible with the pydantic-ai `http_client` seam, or (b) stop passing a stdlib `httpx.AsyncClient` into the anthropic provider when the installed SDK expects its vendored client. This changes the dependency contract / provider construction, so it is a design decision, not a mechanical test fix.\n\n## Evidence\n- Mirror run 33299427686 (dispatched on `main` post-fix): `sweep (macos, full suite)` job 99224621948, `sweep (declared lower-bound resolution)` job 99224621821.\n- `anthropic==1.2.0` shown installing in the macOS leg; error string above aggregated 90x.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] The `Test Suite (mirror)` `sweep (macos, full suite)` and `sweep (declared lower-bound resolution)` legs no longer raise `Invalid http_client argument; Expected ... httpx2.AsyncClient`.\n- [ ] A resolution that floats `anthropic` to its latest (or its declared floor) constructs the Anthropic provider without `TypeError`, on both editable and non-editable installs.\n- [ ] The dependency constraint (or provider-seam change) is portable across CI providers / no CI.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["ci","test-portability","packaging","llm"],"ticket_id":"1f35-74fc-47a0-4d71","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Mirror sweep: unbounded anthropic SDK resolves to 1.2.0 (httpx2) and rejects httpx.AsyncClient on non-editable/floor legs","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["04953580-58b8-4205-9b6c-5c7b9a350074","a815aebe-b319-4319-a886-291b6317e153"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788087222510593001,"uuid":"71396808-5cfd-4d8f-9047-c42b35a7bc62"}